  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday through next Thursday) \nIssued at 1039 PM CDT Thu Aug 27 2026\n\nThe synoptic pattern will gradually shift through the extended as \nthe upper level ridge begins to shift daily, eventually into the \nlower Mississippi River Valley by early next week while flattening \nin response to a deepening trough over the Intermountain West. \nMeanwhile at the surface, southwesterly flow is expected to develop \nas troughing develops in the lee of the Rockies, aiding in a gradual \nuptick in afternoon temperatures through the weekend as thickness \nand heights subtle increase. The warmest temperatures are expected \nto develop Sunday afternoon, where a Heat Advisory may be needed Off \nthe Caprock, as the center of the 595 dam sets up over the South \nPlains region. The upper high will then shift eastward, into the \nArkLaTX region Monday, into the River Valley by mid-week. This will \nallow temperatures to cool slightly, though still quite warm in the \nmid to upper 90s and lower triple digits. Persistent subsidence \nbeneath the ridge will continue to limit convective potential \nthrough the extended, with dry and quiet conditions expected through \nmuch of next week.",
